//www.huffingtonpost.com/2015/0...n_6508790.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 10-25-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:58:43-07:00","id":993086,"title":"","content":"I tried, but the first episode just threw me off. It started an argument between me and my wife about if having sex with the pig was worth it or not, and in general didn't feel like a dystopian at all, just unrealistic hostage negotiation. It did not seem futuristic and had no &quot;twist&quot; I had been looking forward to as part of the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:57:41-07:00","id":993150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993086#post993086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried, but the first episode just threw me off. It started an argument between me and my wife about if having sex with the pig was worth it or not, and in general didn't feel like a dystopian at all, just unrealistic hostage negotiation. It did not seem futuristic and had no &quot;twist&quot; I had been looking forward to as part of the genre.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a weird episode to start with. Most of the show is about technology and theoretical effects on people, in a Twilight Zone-ish fashion. That was more about typically modern, if out there situation regarding social pressure and responsibility and pride. I think just about every episode would offer the same sort of conflict, but be more 'far out.'<br /> <br /> I am curious, who was on which side of the argument?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-25-2016, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:43:58-07:00","id":993191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993150#post993150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a weird episode to start with. Most of the show is about technology and theoretical effects on people, in a Twilight Zone-ish fashion. That was more about typically modern, if out there situation regarding social pressure and responsibility and pride. I think just about every episode would offer the same sort of conflict, but be more 'far out.'<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The first episode was about the public tuning in for the lurid exhibitionism and punishment of watching a politician being raped and forced to commit a rape. That's hyper-realistic to me, as a survivor. &quot;The National Anthem&quot; is one of my favorite episodes, it still haunts me years later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:27:09-07:00","id":993249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993191#post993191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. The first episode was about the public tuning in for the lurid exhibitionism and punishment of watching a politician being raped and forced to commit a rape. That's hyper-realistic to me, as a survivor. &quot;The National Anthem&quot; is one of my favorite episodes, it still haunts me years later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be misremembering. But I thought it was sort of unrealistic that almost none one showed any sympathy or even said &quot;I'mmm so sorry&quot; to him. I feel like if such a thing would happen bin the real world everybody would feel sorry for the man<br /> And only like 7 people would laugh at him . It feels like Black Mirror is trying to tell me &quot;hey Nicky! do you see those people intently watching the guy sufferinggg? That's how people really are. that's the world you live him&quot; And I just don't think that's the truth. I tend to believe there more kindness in this world than that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:00:58-07:00","id":993264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993249#post993249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be misremembering. But I thought it was sort of unrealistic that almost none one showed any sympathy or even said &quot;I'mmm so sorry&quot; to him. I feel like if such a thing would happen bin the real world everybody would feel sorry for the man<br /> And only like 7 people would laugh at him . It feels like Black Mirror is trying to tell me &quot;hey Nicky! do you see those people intently watching the guy sufferinggg? That's how people really are. that's the world you live him&quot; And I just don't think that's the truth. I tend to believe there more kindness in this world than that</div> </div> </div> </div>People laugh about rape every single day. They always have. Always.<br /> <br /> Lawyers call eleven year old gang-rape survivors spiders luring men to their webs.<br /> <br /> People write that journalists nonconsensually recorded naked are &quot;bitches&quot; for suing, and then watch the video illegally online.<br /> <br /> People call survivors sluts, they say he always wants it, they ask her what she was wearing or how drunk she was.<br /> <br /> I was abused starting from the time I was fifteen. Almost ten years later, people very close to me still ask, &quot;hey, do you remember that time you lied about being raped?&quot;<br /> <br /> It is not hard for me, at ALL at all, to imagine a situation where the public would laugh about a politician being raped or forced to commit a rape. With the David Cameron situation, people just laugh. It's about the spectacle. No question about the circumstances. No question about the pressure. Spectacle.<br /> <br /> I hope it's hard for you to imagine because it has never happened to you. I hope that's what it is, and I hope it never does happen to you. It should not happen to anyone. But as someone who has been there, and as someone who reads about it happening every single day, nah. Extremely realistic. Maybe not a pig (though given the Cameron situation, perhaps). Maybe not a pig. But the situation in general? A politician being raped and forced to commit a rape, and people watching in lurid curiosity? Not hard. People watch beheadings online. People watch police shooting people of color. People watch rape at frat parties. People laugh about rape. They do. <br /> <br /> Semi-related, I work closely with an historian of early modern Europe who is currently researching public hangings in 17th and 18th century London. They used to parade (quite literally) convicts through the streets of London, get them drunk, and then hang them as a public sporting type of event for Londoners to watch. Until a wealthier community built up around the tree they used. Then they moved the events to a private space, as the wealthy didn't want it around their communities. Interesting, semi-related thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:42:45-07:00","id":993287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993150#post993150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a weird episode to start with. Most of the show is about technology and theoretical effects on people, in a Twilight Zone-ish fashion. That was more about typically modern, if out there situation regarding social pressure and responsibility and pride. I think just about every episode would offer the same sort of conflict, but be more 'far out.'<br /> <br /> I am curious, who was on which side of the argument?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was against it, realistically there was no proof of her safe return, and he was not obligated to put himself through that for anyone. She felt he was obligated because someone's safety is more important than his humiliation. Near the end I was the most livid I've ever been toward any fictional character, when his wife avoided him. <br /> <br /> I like distopians but for me that episode didn't feel like commentary so much as tragedy porn. I find it so much in media nowadays, it's difficult to avoid it. Whether in superhero stuff like Jessica Jones or the very popular Game of Thrones, it feels a little omnipresent. When I find cool adult content that doesn't add rape in at the first shot (or amazingly at all) that will be my show, but this is too casual with it to enjoy, but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:45:38-07:00","id":993288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993287#post993287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I find cool adult content that doesn't add rape in at the first shot (or amazingly at all) that will be my show, but this is too casual with it to enjoy, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally see where you're coming from. I can't watch GoT anymore because it's so nonchalant. Media with rape is cathartic for me when it's handled well, and I thought this rape was handled well, but I totally get that not everyone might see it that way. If you're interested in watching the show but not episodes with rape, I can let you know which ones have sexually violent content. Remember, it's an anthology, so you don't have to watch them all to enjoy any one episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:09:38-07:00","id":993317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993287#post993287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was against it, realistically there was no proof of her safe return, and he was not obligated to put himself through that for anyone. She felt he was obligated because someone's safety is more important than his humiliation. Near the end I was the most livid I've ever been toward any fictional character, when his wife avoided him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. If I recall his wife was against it from the start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like distopians but for me that episode didn't feel like commentary so much as tragedy porn. I find it so much in media nowadays, it's difficult to avoid it. Whether in superhero stuff like Jessica Jones or the very popular Game of Thrones, it feels a little omnipresent. When I find cool adult content that doesn't add rape in at the first shot (or amazingly at all) that will be my show, but this is too casual with it to enjoy, but that's just me. </div> </div> </div>I know how you feel, especially since some of them are such a slog to sit through for an unsatisfying payoff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:30:09-07:00","id":993328,"title":"","content":"She was, but she should have supported him. I agree he shouldn't have done it, but for her to turn her back when he's hurting like that just struck me to the core. I thought at first she didn't want him to do it for his sake, but it turned out the one person who should have been there for him, wasn't. Just really sad, stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:50:04-07:00","id":993413,"title":"","content":"I'm deeply sorry of hearing that Hayley. i said i thought that episode was unrealistic because i honestly didn't heard anyone blaming the victims for being raped or laughing at themm in a long time. I am sorry that you were abused,i'm glad watching this show is helping you deal with the harm that was done to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:47:45-07:00","id":993451,"title":"","content":"The next one (15 million merits) is, by contrast, probably the most &quot;futuristic&quot; the show's been. Episodes swing wildly between five seconds and five centuries in the future.<br /> <br /> And it's not about hatred of technology. It's about the horror of humanity (mis)using technology.<br /> <br /> A &quot;black mirror&quot; is a smartphone with the power turned off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:40:31-07:00","id":993670,"title":"","content":"I've only gotten to watch one episode so far; Nosedive. It didn't exactly enthrall me; I can get the same terror of social media by reading about Sesame Credit, and it doesn't take nearly so long to get to its exceptionally belaboured point. Like getting hit in the face with a brick scribbled with &quot;SOCIAL MEDIA IS BAD&quot;.<br /> <br /> The message wasn't bad or wrong but, goodness, you could come up with a better way to tell the story. You'd think a story would have the good graces to end when it outright has a character appear just to make the whole thing explicit; like the writer was shouting &quot;HEY, DO YOU GET IT YET!?&quot; at the audience.<br /> <br /> Technology becomes abused because there's something addictive or beneficial about it to <i>someone</i>. Maybe not to everyone, even not to the people using it, but <i>someone</i> is getting something out of it and that someone or someones have to be powerful enough to ensure its spread and compliance. Liking pictures of people's vacations is not even remotely useful to a government or corporation as a measure of someone's social connection or pro-social behaviours, but things like dinging someone for making a scene or rewarding them for being friendly and helpful definitely are. Why not explore that? Why not explore when <i>that</i> is getting abused because that is a very real horror that is ready to explode in the next five to ten years.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, Tom Scott does a better horror story in five minutes than it looks like any of this can do in over an hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:04:55-07:00","id":993723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/990912-everyone-go-watch-black-mirror?p=993670#post993670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only gotten to watch one episode so far; Nosedive. It didn't exactly enthrall me; I can get the same terror of social media by reading about Sesame Credit, and it doesn't take nearly so long to get to its exceptionally belaboured point. Like getting hit in the face with a brick scribbled with &quot;SOCIAL MEDIA IS BAD&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, I didn't think Nosedive was about social media at all. I thought it was about class. I also saw it as more of a social satire than horror, though there were definitely some pretty classical horror elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:09:25-07:00","id":993759,"title":"","content":"It had elements of that, yeah, but also accusations at the shallowness of modern socialization, that social technologies make people more distant, about social conformity, all tied around this central pole of social media making all these things worse the more present it becomes in people's lives.<br /> <br /> That was my take of it, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:14:19-07:00","id":993765,"title":"","content":"I saw the social media criticisms as the surface. The conformity was around class. She even went on a harangue about how you just have to grind as part of the middle class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:38:48-07:00","id":993800,"title":"","content":"i was wondering something about 15 million merits. Was it a criticsm of the x-fator and similar reality shows? like it's saying its wrong that you live in a society where you can only be famous if win a reality instead through your own efforts? And said reality shows not Always judge you by how talented you are. Or is it saying that we live in a world where we forgot to live our own lives and spend all the time looking at tv shows? I agree with the former but not the latter<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","va