ve nothing but disgust and cold hatred for lawyers who act like that, both the defense and the prosecution.<br /> <br /> Where I live, calling someone a &quot;pack of dogs&quot; or a &quot;spider luring men into her web&quot;(especially that one), would lead to scorn from other lawyers and public outrage.<br /> <br /> It is utterly inexcusable. A lawyer should be professional and resolute, not sling around insults in court of all places.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh well, I think this is getting off-topic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}